WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.667
-Christoph, welcome to the show.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:05.601
It is --
It is so great to have you here.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.000
-Thank you.
-Christopher!

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.667
-Wait.
You can yell "Christopher,"

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.400
and you answer to that?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.901
Or did you say
"Christoph Valz"?

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.133
What'd you yell?
-"Christoph Vy."

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.801
-Christoph "Vy" --
"Valts," "Veitz," "Valz"?

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.100
"Veitz," "Valtz."

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.667
-Well,
"Yimmy" Fallon should know.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.100
-Oh, my gosh!
This is ridiculous.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.100
Jimmy, Jimmy.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.434
Thank you
for coming back to the show.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.834
-No, thank you for having me.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:35.968
-I know, you know,
you used to live in New York.

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.634
You were --
-Ah, yes, those were the days.

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:43.067
Actually, lived here during
the beginning of the end.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.634
-What are you talking about?
-Well, I'm talking about

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:50.667
the late '70s and early '80s
of the 20th century.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.701
That's when I was in New York.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.701
-Please.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:57.033
-Now it's trying to be New York.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.300
-What "it's trying
to be New York"?

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.734
No, we are New York.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:04.334
Not trying to be New York.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.601
-Not by comparison.
-Well, I mean --

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.133
-Who's old enough to -- right?

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:12.300
Prove me right.
-I mean, this has happened.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.400
This is New York. I mean,
we were talking back there.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.634
You told me you're not even
a fan of the cold weather.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.868
-Well, cold, yes, that's true.
It's cold.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:22.901
But, you know, I notice --
I wonder, are there stores

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:26.734
where people can go
to get a New York outfit?

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.634
Let me look like a New Yorker.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:31.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:34.267
It really --
Sometimes I feel it's --

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:36.567
They all have
their private costume designers

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:38.000
that say, "No, no, no.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.100
You just look like
a regular person today.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.167
You need to put this on.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.000
You want to look like
a New Yorker.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.400
You're in New York."
You know?

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.334
"That's where the store is
where you go

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:48.234
buy your New Yorker outfit."

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.100
-Yeah. Why are you so worried
and concerned?

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.400
This is -- what you're wearing
is a New Yorker outfit.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.400
-Well, maybe it's envy.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.167
-What are you talking --

00:01:57.167 --> 00:02:00.067
You're envious of other people's
style, sense of style maybe?

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:03.033
-Well, they're really --
a lot of them really look good.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.300
-I know!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.567
But you -- you look good
in everything.

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.567
You were saying backstage to me,
right before the show --

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.534
this is true --
that you were nervous

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.601
even of what jacket to wear.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.267
-Well, because it's cold.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.634
-Yeah,
and you want to look cool.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:18.300
Well, here's the deal.
We have -- I have three jackets.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:22.801
I have one, two --
These are parkas.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:26.100
And we have voting clickers
at our seats.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.267
[ Cheers ]

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.467
The whole night's show

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.367
we're voting on what we like
and don't like.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
Would you like to --

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:35.601
Christoph, would you like
to try on some coats

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:37.367
and see what the audience
likes you in?

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:38.968
-Can we vote about you, too?

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.400
-No, no, no.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.901
Let's start with this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.367
♪♪

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.567
I have these three -- yeah.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.701
♪♪

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.167
We'll come back here.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.400
And we're not sure which one
you want to put on first.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.267
Just these three ones here.
Maybe, yeah.

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:59.133
You want to try that one?
-Okay.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.501
-You pick one.
I'll reintroduce you.

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:02.734
You come out,
and then we'll judge you.

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:04.234
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:05.868
♪♪

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:09.067
Ladies and gentlemen,
Christoph Waltz.

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:14.567
♪♪

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:17.234
[ Laughs ]

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.634
Wow!
Wow!

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.767
Yes.
Yes.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.100
I like that a lot.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.400
This is option number one.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.534
Option number one,
cast your vote.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:30.300
Thumbs up or thumbs down,
option --

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.934
Let's see -- let's see.
The votes are in.

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:35.501
Let's see
what the audience said.

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:36.868
Wow!
That's good.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:39.801
♪♪

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:40.801
That's good.
That's really good.

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:43.033
All right. Ready?
-That's green.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.767
-It actually looks good.
Yes, it's green.

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:45.868
It looks good.
I love this.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.434
-Green steel.
-Yeah, green steel.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:48.667
I love it, it's good.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:49.767
Try -- let's try -- try this.

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.634
We'll try coat number two.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.434
Here we go.
I like this one.

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:55.801
That one's a winner for me.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.567
I like that.
He looked good in that.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.501
I haven't seen that jacket
really so much.

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:00.901
It was kind of different.
I kind of dug it.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:03.267
All right, here we go.
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.467
here in New York,
during the cold weather,

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:08.133
is Christoph Waltz, everyone!

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:09.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:12.300
♪♪

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.534
Oh!
Oh-ho!

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:15.801
That's a stud.

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.634
See, that's
what I'm talking about.

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:20.834
That's a good-looking guy.
I like him.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.367
I like him.
He's kind of --

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.000
You're kind of mysterious.
Almost a --

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.434
-No, orange steel.
-No, I know, orange steel.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.968
I know, but, no, but you also
came out kind of like,

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:29.133
"I don't know
what this guy's deal is.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:30.834
Did he just come off the docks?"

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.133
[ Laughter ]
"Is he a fisherman?"

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.634
I'm just intrigued by him.
I think this one works.

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:36.467
Everyone cast your vote,
thumbs up or thumbs down.

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.067
Be honest.
He can take it.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:41.200
-Don't be honest!
-No, he can handle it.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.534
The votes are in.

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:45.501
Let's see the results on this,
on option number two.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:47.968
Oh, no, wow!
Get -- get out.

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.934
We don't want to see it.
Never happened, never happened.

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.267
The green one's in the lead.

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:52.868
This is the third, and --
That never happened.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.567
All right, here we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.434
This is first time.
This is the best.

00:04:58.434 --> 00:04:59.834
I love it.
All right, here we go.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:02.100
Ladies and gentlemen,
here he is, ready to

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.968
walk down the street
in New York,

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:07.167
in the winter weather,
Christoph Waltz!

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:08.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:13.300
♪♪

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.734
Oh!

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.667
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:22.033
♪♪

00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:24.567
Oh!

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:26.167
[ Laughs ]

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:27.767
I like this one, too.
I like this --

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:29.434
He was definitely mysterious.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:30.934
Like, he kind of had
a little groove to him.

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:32.701
Did a little step,
a little pep in his step.

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:34.634
Everyone take your votes.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:37.000
I think I kind of know
what the winner's gonna to be.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.300
Come on over.
What do you think?

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.801
Christoph,
what are you thinking?

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:43.601
-I think it's, um...

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:46.367
You didn't have a blue one.
I wanted to do my blue steel.

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:47.534
-That's kind of bl--
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:48.901
That is kind of blue.

00:05:48.901 --> 00:05:50.033
That's kind of blue.
All right.

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:53.033
Let's see the results
of this third one.

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:55.634
The third one, the last one,
that is the winner right there!

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:56.901
[ Bell dinging ]

00:05:56.901 --> 00:06:00.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:02.267
Are you gonna --
-Would you come down here,

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:04.868
all the way up there?
The guy with the beard?

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:06.334
Would you come down here,
please?

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:09.434
Quick!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.400
Come, come!
Quick, quick, quick, run, run!

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.834
-Oh, my gosh!
Why, because --

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:19.334
Oh, please.
What in the -- oh, my gosh.

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:22.234
You're getting a jac--
You're getting a coat?

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:24.601
Because you know how to say
it -- pronounce his name?

00:06:24.601 --> 00:06:27.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.300
Off you go.
-Get out of here!

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:34.501
-He could -- He could
pronounce my name properly.

00:06:34.501 --> 00:06:36.734
-Yes, I know.
He could, actually.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:39.033
[ Applause ]
[ Laughs ]

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:42.367
You are the best.
You are the -- we love you.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.701
Wow, that guy is so psyched.
He got a great coat out of this.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:45.901
[ Laughter and cheers ]
-Well, there --

00:06:45.901 --> 00:06:47.701
-That's what you get
for being a fan, right?

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:48.834
Yeah.

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:50.167
-What you get
for saying my name.

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:52.200
-No, I'm sorry.
Christoph.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.467
Let's just --
Can I just call you Christoph?

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:55.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.601 --> 00:06:57.467
Let's talk about...
-If you can say it.

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:59.567
-..."The Consultant."
"The Consultant."

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:03.334
This is a twisty --
a twisty mystery, thriller.

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:04.734
I love it.
-Thank you.

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:06.367
-I don't want
to give anything away.

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:07.868
I don't want to spoil it.
-You couldn't.

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:09.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:11.467
-I could.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.400
I will not, though.
I will not.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.968
-Okay, sorry.
-Well, maybe I can say --

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.601
What could I say?
But you are a consultant.

00:07:18.601 --> 00:07:19.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:22.367
-Well, okay, okay, okay.
We agree on that.

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:27.067
-Shows up after a C.E.O. of
a video-game company is killed.

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:28.968
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:07:28.968 --> 00:07:31.868
And the consultant comes in
and starts making some changes

00:07:31.868 --> 00:07:33.801
that not everyone's happy about.

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:35.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.868 --> 00:07:38.934
You are ruthless!

00:07:38.934 --> 00:07:41.067
You are sinister!

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:43.534
-"Sinister" is a beautiful word.
-Thank you.

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:44.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.701 --> 00:07:47.033
Is it fair to say
you are a villain?

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:49.534
-A what?

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:51.601
-Are you --
Are you a villain in this?

00:07:51.601 --> 00:07:53.167
-No.

00:07:53.167 --> 00:07:56.133
[ Laughter ]
Um, w-why?

00:07:56.133 --> 00:07:58.734
-You know --
-I said you couldn't, really,

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:01.567
and I was right.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.567 --> 00:08:03.334
-I think I set it up
pretty well, right?

00:08:03.334 --> 00:08:05.067
You guys know what it's about,
kind of?

00:08:05.067 --> 00:08:07.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:07.667 --> 00:08:08.834
-Okay.
-All right?

00:08:08.834 --> 00:08:09.901
-Okay.
-All right, good.

00:08:09.901 --> 00:08:11.567
Have I said enough?
-Sure.

00:08:11.567 --> 00:08:13.133
-I want to show a clip.

00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:16.300
Here's Christoph Waltz
in "The Consultant."

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.667
-Not bad.
-Not bad?

00:08:17.667 --> 00:08:19.501
-No, for a start.
-Take a look.

00:08:19.501 --> 00:08:21.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:24.067
-Good morning, comrades.

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:30.167
Unfortunately, Mr. Sang
cannot be with us today,

00:08:30.167 --> 00:08:32.367
but he sends his best regards.

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:35.767
[ Quiet gasps, murmurs ]

00:08:35.767 --> 00:08:37.801
To the wonderful faces
I see below,

00:08:37.801 --> 00:08:42.501
thank you for being an important
part in Compware's success.

00:08:42.501 --> 00:08:47.267
I'm looking forward to getting
to know you all personally.

00:08:47.267 --> 00:08:50.501
You're valued.

00:08:50.501 --> 00:08:55.334
And for those who work remotely,

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:58.634
you have exactly one hour
to get here in person,

00:08:58.634 --> 00:09:02.000
or your contracts of employment
will be terminated.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.234
That's all.

00:09:10.234 --> 00:09:12.033
-Yeah!
That's how do you do it!

00:09:12.033 --> 00:09:13.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:13.334 --> 00:09:15.033
Christoph Waltz, everybody!

00:09:15.033 --> 00:09:19.701
"The Consultant" premieres
February 24th on Prime Video!

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:21.300
Tig Notaro
joins us after the break.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.801
Stick around.

